Let F=\{x:c(x)=0,\ g(x)\le0\} and  ar x\in F. A family \{
abla c_i( ar x)\}_{i\in I}\cup\{
abla g_j( ar x)\}_{j\in J}, where I\subseteq\{1,\ldots,m\} and J\subseteq A( ar x), is positively linearly dependent if coefficients \alpha_i\in\mathbb R and  eta_j\ge0, not all zero, satisfy \sum_{i\in I}\alpha_i
abla c_i( ar x)+\sum_{j\in J} eta_j
abla g_j( ar x)=0. CPLD holds at  ar x if every such positively dependent family remains linearly dependent throughout some neighborhood of  ar x.

Let F=\{x:c(x)=0,\ g(x)\le0\} and  ar x\in F. RCPLD holds at  ar x if the equality-gradient rank is constant near  ar x and there is an index set I selecting a basis of \operatorname{span}\{
abla c_i( ar x)\}_{i=1}^m such that, for every J\subseteq A( ar x), positive linear dependence of \{
abla c_i( ar x)\}_{i\in I}\cup\{
abla g_j( ar x)\}_{j\in J} implies linear dependence of \{
abla c_i(x)\}_{i\in I}\cup\{
abla g_j(x)\}_{j\in J} throughout some neighborhood of  ar x.

Let \(c:\mathbb R^n	o\mathbb R^m\) and \(g:\mathbb R^n	o\mathbb R^p\) be continuously differentiable, let \(F=\{x\in\mathbb R^n:c(x)=0,\ g(x)\le 0\}\), let \( ar x\in F\), and define \(A( ar x)=\{j\in\{1,\ldots,p\}:g_j( ar x)=0\}\) and \(v(x)=\|c(x)\|_1+\|[g(x)]_+\|_1\). LICQ means that \(\{
abla c_i( ar x):1\le i\le m\}\cup\{
abla g_j( ar x):j\in A( ar x)\}\) is linearly independent. MFCQ means that \(\{
abla c_i( ar x):1\le i\le m\}\) is linearly independent and there exists \(d\in\mathbb R^n\) such that \(
abla c_i( ar x)^	op d=0\) for every \(i\) and \(
abla g_j( ar x)^	op d<0\) for every \(j\in A( ar x)\). LICQ implies MFCQ, and MFCQ implies that there exist \(\kappa>0\) and \(\delta>0\) such that \(\operatorname{dist}(x,F)\le \kappa v(x)\) whenever \(\|x- ar x\|<\delta\).
